## R2.1 (B2) — union narrowing acceptance smoke.
##
## A union value `x: Int | String = 5` is stored as B1's runtime tagged
## `{tag@0, payload@1}` cell (tag = fnv1a_hash("Int")). `if x is Int` must:
##   1. prove the tag at runtime — MIR emits `load@0 == fnv1a("Int")` (Step D),
##   2. narrow `x` to `Int` in the THEN branch (Steps A/B typecheck facts), and
##   3. recover the underlying value via the offset-1 payload load (Step E).
##
## The first runtime-observable union READ. If narrowing recovers the member
## value, the THEN branch returns 5 (NOT the fall-through 99). Standalone
## (not qspec) so a real compile/run exercises the codegen path.
##
## Compile + run:
##   ./self-hosted/bin/quartz spec/qz/union_narrow_smoke.qz > /tmp/un.ll
##   llc /tmp/un.ll -filetype=obj -o /tmp/un.o
##   clang /tmp/un.o -o /tmp/un -lm -lpthread && /tmp/un; echo "exit=$?"
## Expected: prints "recovered 5" and exits 5.

def main(): Int
  var x: Int | String = 5
  if x is Int
    puts("recovered #{str_from_int(x)}")
    return x
  end
  puts("FAIL: is Int did not narrow")
  return 99
end
